<section class="lp-band lp-between" aria-labelledby="between-title">
  <div class="lp-section">
    <div class="lp-intro">
      <h2 id="between-title">Everything between the idea and the day.</h2>
      <p>Planning Center knows who’s in your church. It’ll check them in when they arrive. The weeks of planning in between have been running on email, a spreadsheet and a group text. That’s the part Flockwork takes.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="lp-track" data-controller="reveal">
      <li class="lp-track-end lp-track-start"><b>Your people</b> <span class="lp-track-chips"><span>Planning Center</span><span>Breeze</span><span>CSV</span></span></li>
      <li class="lp-track-step" style="--i: 1">Plan it</li>
      <li class="lp-track-step" style="--i: 2">Bring the team</li>
      <li class="lp-track-step" style="--i: 3">Send one link</li>
      <li class="lp-track-step" style="--i: 4">Watch the spots fill</li>
      <li class="lp-track-card">
        <span class="lp-badge">Flockwork</span>
        <h3>The planning</h3>
        <ul class="lp-track-list">
          <li><%= planner_tool_icon("signup_sheet", size: 20) %>Who’s bringing what</li>
          <li><%= planner_tool_icon("tasks", size: 20) %>Who owns which task</li>
          <li><%= planner_tool_icon("schedule", size: 20) %>When setup starts, and where</li>
          <li><%= planner_tool_icon("budget", size: 20) %>What it’s costing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>One project everyone can see, instead of six places to look.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="lp-track-end lp-track-finish"><b>The day</b> Registration and check-in, back where it was</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="lp-track-note">Your people come in from Planning Center or a CSV, so nobody types a roster twice.</p>
  </div>
</section>
